WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.900
Put a bacterium beside
one of your own cells,

2
00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:04.450
at the same scale.

3
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.170
It is dwarfed.

4
00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:10.260
Inside your cell, the DNA
is locked away in a nucleus,

5
00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:12.380
wrapped in a double membrane.

6
00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:14.780
A bacterium has no nucleus.

7
00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:18.810
Yet it still has DNA, and
still makes its own proteins.

8
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:21.530
So where does a bacterium keep its genes,

9
00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.820
and what else does it manage without?

10
00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:27.960
In this mission, you'll compare a
bacterium with one of your own cells,

11
00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:29.690
feature by feature.

12
00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:32.910
Then you'll find out why a
bacterium needs its wall,

13
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:36.150
and what happens in water
when it is stripped away.

14
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:40.120
Your mission: find out where
a bacterium keeps its genes,

15
00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:41.800
and what it manages without.
